With MSTest 3.8.2+ and constructor injection, here's the recommended pattern:

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class MyTests : IAsyncInitialization, IAsyncDisposable
{
    private readonly TestContext _testContext;
    private HttpClient _client;

    // Constructor injection for TestContext (sync setup)
    public MyTests(TestContext testContext)
    {
        _testContext = testContext;
        // Lightweight sync initialization here
    }

    // Async initialization (runs before each test)
    public async Task InitializeAsync()
    {
        _client = new HttpClient();
        await _client.GetAsync("https://example.com/warmup");
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public async Task MyTest()
    {
        _testContext.WriteLine("Running test...");
        // test logic
    }

    // Async cleanup
    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        if (_client is not null)
            await CastAndDispose(_client);
    }

    private static async ValueTask CastAndDispose(IDisposable d)
    {
        if (d is IAsyncDisposable ad)
            await ad.DisposeAsync();
        else
            d.Dispose();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- **Constructor** receives `TestContext` via DI — no `[TestInitialize]` needed for context access
- **`IAsyncInitialization`** — implement `InitializeAsync()` for async setup (replaces `[TestInitialize] async Task`)
- **`IAsyncDisposable`** — for async teardown
- You can also still use `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` if you prefer attributes over interfaces
